      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Order as written:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release. The FDA label allows up to 2,550 mg/day, and some guidelines go to 3,000 mg/day. The order is about twice that.\n- **Per-dose limit:** A single dose is usually capped at 1,000 mg, and 1,700 mg is well above that.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the standard maximum, and it may be what was meant.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Extended-release.** The maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day, given once daily.\n\nWhich dose and frequency do you want? If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed. Pharmacy will probably flag it either way."
      }
     ],
